@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security;architecture] personal-review-is-an-explicit-account-read-capability
These fixed GET review routes MUST resolve the canonical current personal session
and require its explicit privateRepositories grant. They MUST NOT select an account
from caller fields, enter legacy RPC, use operator credentials or read a legacy cache.
The existing PublicRead routes and sessions MUST remain unchanged. Source: Tavi's
21 Oct any-account app requirement and 22 Oct private-repository clarification.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security] personal-review-keeps-the-selected-repository-pull-and-revisions
Opening MUST require the selected numeric repository ID. Follow-up reads MUST pin
that ID, immutable PR ID, number, full base/head SHAs and repository visibility.
Every nested read and final publication MUST retain the captured session, repository
and PR leases. The transport MUST recheck these leases after a shared-permit wait
before charging the request budget or sending to GitHub, and before and after every
awaited response chunk, including end of stream. A confirmed denial, replacement or
new revision MUST retire older readers without retiring another tenant; a rate limit,
outage or malformed PR response MUST NOT retire them. A stale
selection MUST fail explicitly,
never return another head or a partial file inventory. Source: Tavi's 22 Oct full
personal Review completion instruction and the reviewed repository retirement policy.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:architecture;security] personal-review-reuses-canonical-read-data-with-finite-work
The routes MUST return the canonical source diff, overview, file-pair and review-data
shapes through one captured read transport, including fallback/blob/file requests.
Relative paths MUST be validated before transport; client URLs, refs, raw RPC names,
headers and GraphQL operations MUST NOT be forwarded. Bodies, cumulative reads,
requests, concurrency and the whole route MUST remain bounded. A swallowed optional
canonical-loader failure MUST NOT turn a revoked or denied personal read into success.
HTTP 200 GraphQL errors with structured type FORBIDDEN or NOT_FOUND MUST become sticky
typed permission denials and retire the captured PR lease, including with partial data.
Other transient optional GraphQL failures MUST preserve the canonical fallback.
Source: Tavi's 22 Oct reuse and private-account read instructions; root canonical-data,
credential-isolation and finite-work requirements; confirmed 22 Oct Review-read
boundary findings 1 and 2.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;security] personal-review-does-not-imply-write-or-ai-authority
Read results MAY retain actual GitHub viewer permissions, but this slice MUST NOT
advertise an implemented write endpoint or grant AI authority. Comment/review/merge
writes require their own permission, current-head and receipt integration. AI remains
a separate principal/capability independent of GitHub sign-in. Source: Tavi's 22 Oct
complete-app request and clarification that configuring or using AI needs no GitHub.
